Disable the HDF5 ROS3 (read-only S3) virtual file driver.

ROS3 pulls in libcurl + openssl and, through them, a large static dependency
chain (brotli, nghttp2, idn2, gpgme, libgcrypt, ...). That chain does not link
cleanly under the mingw toolchain on Windows and is not needed by consumers that
read local HDF5 files. Turning it off removes the curl/openssl dependency
entirely so downstream packages (rhdf5) link with just zlib.

--- a/tools/hdf5_setup.R
+++ b/tools/hdf5_setup.R
@@ -24,5 +24,5 @@
     HDF5_ENABLE_Z_LIB_SUPPORT="ON",
     HDF5_ENABLE_SZIP_SUPPORT="ON",
     HDF5_USE_LIBAEC_STATIC="ON",
-    HDF5_ENABLE_ROS3_VFD="ON",
+    HDF5_ENABLE_ROS3_VFD="OFF",
     NULL
